v1.0.0 — MVP: Student Attendance Management Portal

Release-ready functional baseline, closing the MVP scope frozen in Task 1.

Capabilities
- Role-based login for ADMIN, FACULTY and STUDENT, with BCrypt-hashed credentials.
- Attendance capture for a course session: full roster in one screen, defaulting
  to PRESENT, refusing a future session date, and editing rather than duplicating
  when a session is reopened.
- Paged records list, and search combining roll number, course, date range and
  workflow state in any subset.
- Role-based approval workflow DRAFT -> SUBMITTED -> APPROVED | REJECTED, with
  APPROVED terminal and every transition refused at the service layer rather than
  hidden in the UI. Only an ADMIN may approve or reject; rejection requires a remark.
- Summary dashboard with attendance percentage per student per course computed
  from approved records only, below-threshold students flagged against a
  configurable threshold, and counts per workflow state.
- Students see only their own attendance, resolved from the authenticated

